A||N||18||bHooper||Do Fiero's have a personality?||||3
Z||000000||bHooper||10-01-1999||02:26 PM||||Last nite my girlfriend stated that she didn't understand how a person could have a pasion or compasion for something that didn't have a personality (meaning a fiero).  She said that unlike a horse, a fiero doesn't think on it's own...it does'nt make decisions  for itself.  I told her that fiero's are full of personality and constantly make decisions without any human input.  I see where she is coming from, but unfortunately can't currently back up my side as my car is being restored at the moment.  I believe that once she is able to take a ride in my GT, she will change her mind.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Any one have any thought's or comments about this?<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 10-01-1999).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||88 Fiero||10-01-1999||06:33 PM||||Personality on a Fiero...I think when you look at different Fiero's you will see that each one of this car's has been customize by their owners. Some have different front facia and body styles while others have the stock body. Others prefer V8's for brute force and others prefer the Stock engine. With these customization the car has been personalize accordingly by their owners.And it shows it's own personality...||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||10-01-1999||08:10 PM||||Fiero's do have personality. For instance. My Fiero has a big dent on it's front bumper. And they do make decisions on their own. I was backing out of my parking spot when my Fiero decided to break a ball joint. What was it thinking?||||reg||7
Z||000003||Greg Piet||10-01-1999||08:36 PM||||Well have your girlfriend watch the movie "Christine", that seems like the extreme case of how a car could have a personality.<BR>I know one of my previous cars that I babied severely, would not start or run for my ex.  It was a bit finnicky and required the right touch, but its behavior had my ex convinced that my car didnt like her.<BR>Even if I started it, and then she got behind the wheel it would die.  It was an automatic, so i cant say it was because she didnt know how to drive stick.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eddie||10-01-1999||08:51 PM||||I think the pasion make's the personality come to life!!!	<BR>						Eddie||||reg||1
Z||000005||fastonpumpgas||10-01-1999||09:55 PM||||My girlfriend wont even try to beat my fiero in respect, I love her , the car that is, And she knows it .  as for personality, Its has tons.  Doesnt have alot of mods yet, but there is no other car like it.  And the only way you would know that is if you were a fiero owner..  I say  " KEEP THE CAR !!! "||||reg||1
Z||000006||CUTTER||10-01-1999||10:59 PM||||My car is my girlfriend, we make out and everything J/K. My car is my best friend though, knowone can tell my car what to do. It does what I say and when I say. Thats what makes it my best friend. hehe it sounds pathetic but its true!||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||10-02-1999||01:27 AM||||Today was like one of those days when several playground bullies tried to push you off the slide,but in this case it was my Fiero;went for a drive to a friends house,on the way some idiot darn near ran me off the road,changing lanes into mine,then,on the way home,another one did a similar thing,only head on!(swerve,swerve again)<BR>Then some woman in a black,full length coat ran in front of my car.(slam on brakes,watch her goofy male companion leer at my car).<P>I wish all these wonderful people could occupy the very same place at the same time,far away from where I happen to be.<P>Anyways,this has all given my Fiero a complex,and I fear that something like in "Christine" will happen if she doesn't get help soon,should probably remove the battery,just to be safe.It could possibly have something to do with the car'past duty as a police cruiser(pent up aggression).<BR>Who knows?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000008||bHooper||10-04-1999||07:35 AM||||Well, apparently there are 2 methods of thought regarding "personality" with Fiero's.  Some have refered to the physical adornment that many owners have performed on their cars.... but a few people have mentioned the sick tantric ability of fiero being able to make their own decisions.  An example, when my car decided to brake the pressure plated so it could pull out into the busy intersection without my control...or the time it it told me to change the struts, tires and brakes after pulling a multiple 360 degree spins..or locked its doors with the keys inside.<P>These are the types of "self awareness" that I was looking for.<P>Brian||||reg||6
Z||000009||ChadMan||10-04-1999||09:27 AM||||Anyone who's seen Herbie the Love Bug knows cars have personalities - especially unique cars like Fieros.  (You can decide if I'm kidding or not.)<P>The interesting thing about Fieros is that no two are ever the same - even two from the same year with the same drivetrain and option packages.||||reg||10
Z||000010||Dan||10-04-1999||09:49 AM|||| I'm forty-three years old and in all my infinate wisdom, I say dump the broad.She obviously has no compassion nor comprehension<BR>of the human male beast.How would your children  grow-up? After being a sailor for seven years, I can guarantee ships have a mighty personality, and each their own.I can't understand anyone not being receptive to the vibrations.Is this girl a blonde? If she has any compassion at all, maybe she could tell you why all sailors lovingly refer to their ships as she.No, its not because they are broad in the middle.Is this the woman you want to spend the rest of your life with? Run, BHOPPER, run!We can all remember the cars we got rid of and really loved. Put your girlfriend on notice. Hey, really, I'm just kidding,really.The simple, naked truth is..."sure." ||||reg||1
