Z||000018||batboy||10-05-1999||11:34 PM||||My V8 Fiero that I bought last spring was an unfinished project, sort of like a half wild horse that had been abused. (The previous owner was a good ol' boy ex-stock car driver so you can imagine he ran the guano out of it.) I had to work on it all day in his drveway when I bought it before I felt it could handle the drive home.<P>Once home, I worked on it some more and some more. For a while, it would break down on everyother test drive. Numerous bolts were loose all over the car. Electrical problems up the waazoo. I'd fix one thing and find something else wrong.<P>Slowly, I've nursed it back to health. Now the car is beginning to show it's appreciation, because it's been a long while since it broke down. I guess if you spend enough time, money, and love on them, they start loving you back.<P>I took the long scenic way home tonight from work. Both the Fiero and I were happy. The car was running smooth, powerful, very graceful and I had a big grin on my face. Yes, Fieros can have a personality.||||reg||1
